WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.680
As a choreographer,
I find inspiration in my head.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.760
I am inspired by the space,
the people, the stage.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:30.480
For me, it’s important to lead workshops
and show that we are independent in our work.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.480
I think it is important
for disabled artists

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.600
from other places

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.720
to come together.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:50.800
Firstly, because they can
exchange their experiences,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.440
maybe I should say ‘we’ can exchange
‘our’ experience.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.000
We can learn so much from each other.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.720
Disabled people should lead more workshops,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:20.840
because I think disabled people's work
is often neglected.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:27.960
I have the feeling that these people
are excluded from society

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:34.080
and that they can't show their work.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:40.080
I think non-disabled people
should work with disabled people.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:46.440
And vice versa. Disabled people should work
with non-disabled people.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:54.160
This way, they can watch
each other's work

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:59.720
and they can see what is useful for each group
and use it in each project.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:09.080
I really enjoy doing my job
as a choreographer.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.520
I don't really see myself
as a disabled choreographer.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.640
What really strikes me is that there are
lots of people who want to achieve new things.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.120
They really push themselves
to achieve new things.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.520
And it's really nice to see
what other people do.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:33.400
Artists with disability
should lead workshops

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:43.760
because in that way they can collaborate
with others and present themselves.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.600
I think that artists with disabilities

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:55.920
should lead workshops
and make performances.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.200
I was dancing with Vivi
and with the teacher.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.720
I showed them my moves,
how to move slowly.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:11.080
I showed them this way,
from one shoulder to the other,

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.480
then we rotated around the back

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.760
and came together.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.680
When I dance, everybody understands me.

